1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,900
Three brothers shook
three lots in a helmet.

2
00:00:03,160 --> 00:00:06,000
Whatever each of them drew,
he would rule it forever.

3
00:00:06,600 --> 00:00:11,760
To understand how the universe came to be
divided that way, start with their father.

4
00:00:12,780 --> 00:00:15,660
Cronus ruled everything,
and Cronus was afraid.

5
00:00:16,280 --> 00:00:19,380
He had been told that one of his
children would overthrow him,

6
00:00:19,380 --> 00:00:22,160
exactly as he had
overthrown his own father.

7
00:00:22,440 --> 00:00:24,240
So he found a solution.

8
00:00:24,780 --> 00:00:28,920
Every time his wife Rhea gave birth,
he took the child and swallowed it.

9
00:00:29,200 --> 00:00:30,160
Hestia.

10
00:00:30,160 --> 00:00:31,160
Demeter.

11
00:00:31,320 --> 00:00:32,300
Hera.

12
00:00:32,300 --> 00:00:32,580
Hades.

13
00:00:32,580 --> 00:00:33,580
Poseidon.

14
00:00:33,840 --> 00:00:36,160
Five children, alive, inside him.

15
00:00:36,700 --> 00:00:38,940
When the sixth was coming, Rhea hid.

16
00:00:39,000 --> 00:00:40,860
She gave birth in a cave on Crete,

17
00:00:40,860 --> 00:00:44,180
and handed her husband a stone
wrapped in a baby's blanket.

18
00:00:44,280 --> 00:00:46,360
He swallowed it without looking.

19
00:00:46,920 --> 00:00:48,600
The child was Zeus.

20
00:00:49,220 --> 00:00:53,060
Grown, he came back and forced his father
to bring up everything he had eaten.

21
00:00:53,380 --> 00:00:55,020
The stone came first.

22
00:00:55,080 --> 00:00:59,020
Then his brothers and sisters,
one at a time, undamaged.

23
00:00:59,780 --> 00:01:05,640
What followed was a war that lasted ten
years, and neither side could finish it.

24
00:01:06,300 --> 00:01:08,360
So Zeus went down into the pit beneath the

25
00:01:08,360 --> 00:01:10,840
world and let out the
prisoners kept there.

26
00:01:11,460 --> 00:01:15,300
Three one-eyed smiths made the
weapons: a thunderbolt for Zeus,

27
00:01:15,300 --> 00:01:20,460
a trident for Poseidon, and for Hades
a cap that made its wearer invisible.

28
00:01:20,660 --> 00:01:23,460
Three giants with a hundred
arms each ended the fighting,

29
00:01:23,460 --> 00:01:26,200
and the Titans took
their place in the pit.

30
00:01:26,800 --> 00:01:28,800
And then the winners had a problem.

31
00:01:29,020 --> 00:01:33,120
They had won a universe, and no
agreement about who owned it.

32
00:01:33,820 --> 00:01:35,540
They did not fight over it.

33
00:01:35,540 --> 00:01:37,680
According to Homer, they drew lots.

34
00:01:37,980 --> 00:01:39,440
Poseidon drew the sea.

35
00:01:39,560 --> 00:01:41,800
Hades drew the mist and the dark.

36
00:01:41,860 --> 00:01:43,800
Zeus drew the wide sky.

37
00:01:44,280 --> 00:01:47,140
One part was left out
of the draw on purpose.

38
00:01:47,260 --> 00:01:51,060
The earth, and Olympus itself,
stayed common to all three.

39
00:01:51,320 --> 00:01:55,380
The place they all cared about
most was the one place nobody won.

40
00:01:56,380 --> 00:02:00,300
Zeus took the sky, and with it
something more useful than weather.

41
00:02:00,980 --> 00:02:04,517
He became the god of the oath
and of the stranger at the door

42
00:02:04,517 --> 00:02:08,340
— the rules that let strangers
deal with each other at all.

43
00:02:08,600 --> 00:02:11,140
His weapon had been a gift from prisoners.

44
00:02:11,300 --> 00:02:14,360
His real power was the arrangement itself.

45
00:02:15,580 --> 00:02:18,420
Poseidon drew more of the world's
surface than either brother,

46
00:02:18,420 --> 00:02:20,660
and never accepted the result.

47
00:02:21,280 --> 00:02:24,480
In the Iliad he tells a
messenger that they drew equally,

48
00:02:24,480 --> 00:02:28,560
that they are equals, and that Zeus
has no right to give him orders.

49
00:02:29,140 --> 00:02:32,820
Then he backs down,
because Zeus is the elder.

50
00:02:33,320 --> 00:02:34,700
Which is strange.

51
00:02:34,880 --> 00:02:37,840
Hesiod has Zeus born last of the six.

52
00:02:38,440 --> 00:02:40,720
Neither poem explains the difference.

53
00:02:41,020 --> 00:02:42,460
Hades drew worst.

54
00:02:42,740 --> 00:02:46,240
He got the dead, and a
kingdom with no sky in it.

55
00:02:46,260 --> 00:02:50,460
He does not live on Olympus, and he is
not one of the twelve who sit there.

56
00:02:51,000 --> 00:02:56,250
The Greeks were uneasy enough about him
that they mostly avoided saying his name,

57
00:02:56,250 --> 00:03:00,219
and built him almost nothing
under that name — one sanctuary,

58
00:03:00,219 --> 00:03:04,460
opened one day a year, with
only the priest allowed inside.

59
00:03:05,360 --> 00:03:07,780
What they called him instead was Plouton.

60
00:03:08,780 --> 00:03:09,960
The rich one.

61
00:03:10,280 --> 00:03:12,640
Because the dead were
not all he had drawn.

62
00:03:12,800 --> 00:03:15,454
Everything that comes out
of the ground comes out

63
00:03:15,454 --> 00:03:18,213
of his kingdom — the silver
in the mines, the gold,

64
00:03:18,213 --> 00:03:22,700
and the seed that goes under the soil
in autumn and comes back up in spring.

65
00:03:23,620 --> 00:03:27,460
The brother who drew the darkness ended
up holding the wealth of the world.

66
00:03:27,460 --> 00:03:32,820
And every person who has ever lived
arrives, eventually, in his share of it.

67
00:03:33,440 --> 00:03:36,040
Three brothers divided
the universe and left

68
00:03:36,040 --> 00:03:38,980
the ground we live on common to all three.

69
00:03:39,800 --> 00:03:43,844
In the next part, their three sisters
— swallowed by the same father,

70
00:03:43,844 --> 00:03:47,480
freed by the same brother,
and given no kingdom at all.

71
00:03:48,180 --> 00:03:52,780
Sky, sea, or the dead — which
lot would you have wanted?

72
00:03:53,600 --> 00:03:55,200
Tell us in the comments.

73
00:03:55,200 --> 00:03:59,640
If you like stories like this one, leave
a like and subscribe to Animated Tales.

74
00:04:00,120 --> 00:04:01,398
Until next time.
